### DevNest API — Request Collection
### Use with VS Code "REST Client" extension (humao.rest-client) or JetBrains' built-in HTTP client.
### Click "Send Request" above any request block below. No Postman needed.
###
### AUTH NOTE: This project now uses cookie-based sessions (Redis), not JWT Bearer tokens.
### After you run Register or Login below, the REST Client extension automatically stores the
### Set-Cookie response and resends it on every later request in THIS FILE — no manual copying,
### no @token variable, no Authorization header needed anywhere. Just run Register/Login once,
### then run any other request below in the same file and the cookie goes along for free.
### (If a request stops being authenticated, it usually means the session expired or you
### restarted the Redis container — just re-run Login again.)

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000/api/v1

### Variables you'll still fill in manually — these are just ids, not auth.
@userId = 77131d8d-ac94-4c43-876c-82747466380e
@otherUserId = 0ba5faae-9ba5-46f0-921e-f9a536890c51
@projectId = c37512a8-c08d-495c-93c2-0c66fab84027
@skillId = 08de9af2-06c6-44c0-94c0-75ab40a3b630
@commentId = PASTE_COMMENT_ID_HERE
@username = omar_test2

###############################################
### AUTH
###############################################

### Register — also logs you in (sets the session cookie)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "omar_test2",
  "email": "omar_test2@example.com",
  "password": "SuperSecret123!"
}

### Login — sets the session cookie. Run this whenever the session expires.
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "omar_test2@example.com",
  "password": "SuperSecret123!"
}

### ^ Check the response headers here for "Set-Cookie: sessionId=...". If it's missing,
### something's wrong (check the `secure` flag isn't forcing HTTPS-only in local dev).

###############################################
### USER
###############################################

### Get current user (me) — no Authorization header needed, cookie handles it
GET {{baseUrl}}/user/me

### Update current user (me)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/user/me
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bio": "Backend dev, Prisma enjoyer."
}

### Get another user's profile by id (respects isPublic)
GET {{baseUrl}}/user/{{otherUserId}}

### Get a user's projects by username (respects isPublic + owner bypass + Redis cache)
GET {{baseUrl}}/user/{{username}}/projects

### Get a user's skills by username (respects isPublic + owner bypass)
GET {{baseUrl}}/user/{{username}}/skills

###############################################
### PROJECTS
###############################################

### Create a project
# @name createProject
POST {{baseUrl}}/projects
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Test Project",
  "description": "A project created for testing.",
  "status": "in progress",
  "isPublic": true
}

### ^ Copy the returned "id" into @projectId above.

### Get one project by id (respects isPublic + owner bypass)
GET {{baseUrl}}/projects/{{projectId}}

### Update a project (must be owner) — should also invalidate the projects cache
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/projects/{{projectId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "completed"
}

### Delete a project (must be owner) — should also invalidate the projects cache
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/projects/{{projectId}}

### Get comments on a project
GET {{baseUrl}}/projects/{{projectId}}/comments

###############################################
### SKILLS
###############################################

### Create a skill
# @name createSkill
POST {{baseUrl}}/skills
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "PostgreSQL",
  "level": "INTERMEDIATE"
}

### ^ Copy the returned "id" into @skillId above.

### Get one skill by id (respects owner's isPublic)
GET {{baseUrl}}/skills/{{skillId}}

### Update a skill (must be owner)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/skills/{{skillId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "level": "ADVANCED"
}

### Delete a skill (must be owner)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/skills/{{skillId}}

###############################################
### COMMENTS
###############################################

### Add a comment to a project
# @name createComment
POST {{baseUrl}}/comments
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "content": "Really cool project!",
  "projectId": "{{projectId}}"
}

### ^ Copy the returned "id" into @commentId above.

### Get one comment by id (respects the project's visibility rules)
GET {{baseUrl}}/comments/{{commentId}}

### Update a comment (must be owner)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/comments/{{commentId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "content": "Updated comment text."
}

### Delete a comment (must be owner)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/comments/{{commentId}}

###############################################
### STARS
###############################################

### Star a project
POST {{baseUrl}}/projects/{{projectId}}/star

### Unstar a project
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/projects/{{projectId}}/star

###############################################
### SESSION-SPECIFIC CHECKS (new — worth running these specifically)
###############################################

### Confirm the cookie round-trip actually works at all:
### 1. Run Login above.
### 2. Look at the response headers for "Set-Cookie: sessionId=...; HttpOnly; ...".
### 3. Run the request below with NOTHING else changed — no header added by you.
###    If this succeeds, the browser/REST Client -> cookie -> authMiddleware -> Redis
###    round trip is genuinely working end to end.
GET {{baseUrl}}/user/me

### Confirm invalidation still works after switching to cookies:
### create a project, then re-fetch the owner's project list twice — second call should
### be a cache hit (check server logs for "Cache hit" / no Prisma query logged).
GET {{baseUrl}}/user/{{username}}/projects

###############################################
### SECURITY / EDGE CASE CHECKS
### Worth running these deliberately — they're the ones we found bugs in tonight.
###############################################

### Try to view a PRIVATE project you don't own -> should be 401/403, not the data
GET {{baseUrl}}/projects/{{projectId}}

### Try to view a comment on someone else's PRIVATE project -> should be blocked
GET {{baseUrl}}/comments/{{commentId}}

### Try to update/delete something you don't own -> should be 401/403
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/projects/{{projectId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Hijack attempt"
}

### Try to star your own project -> should be 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/projects/{{projectId}}/star

### Try to star the same project twice -> should be 409 Conflict
POST {{baseUrl}}/projects/{{projectId}}/star

### Hit a route with NO cookie at all -> should be 401 unauthenticated.
### The REST Client extension only omits the cookie if you never ran Login in this file,
### or if you're using a fresh/incognito-style request — otherwise it's hard to simulate
### "no cookie" from within the same file. Easiest way to really test this one: open the
### app in an actual browser's private/incognito window and hit an authenticated route
### with no prior login there.
GET {{baseUrl}}/user/me

### Hit a route with a malformed UUID param -> should be a clean 400, not a raw crash
GET {{baseUrl}}/projects/not-a-real-uuid
